course: dictionary
lesson: 170
title: Agile and quick
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Agile means able to move quickly, easily and lightly. A gymnast, a goalkeeper or a cat that leaps and turns fast is agile.
explain: Agile can also describe a mind. «An agile mind» is a mind that thinks quickly and cleverly. Look at the words around the word for clues: leaps, climbs and dodges point to moving, and quick thinking points to the mind.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Cats are quick and good at balancing, and they often survive falls» still makes sense, so agile fits. In work and computing, agile means a team working in short steps and changing plans often.
fact: Agile means able to move quickly, easily and lightly.
fact: «Agile» can also mean able to think quickly and cleverly, as in «an agile mind».
fact: «Agility training» helps people move more quickly and easily in sport.
fact: In work, «agile» means working in teams in short steps and changing plans often.
fact: Agile is an adjective: agile, more agile, most agile.
exercise: «The agile monkey swung from branch to branch.» What does agile mean here? | Angry and loud | Large and heavy | Very sleepy | *Able to move quickly and easily
exercise: Mia says «an agile mind» means a slow, careless mind. What does agile mean in «an agile mind»? | Full of noise | Heavy and tired | *Able to think quickly and cleverly | Slow and careful
exercise: Which word in «Cats are agile and often survive falls» means quick and good at balancing? | *agile | Cats | falls | scrapes
test: Ben says agile in a team plan means very old. What does agile mean when a team works in short steps and changes plans often? | *Working in short steps and changing plans often | Bad at team games | Very old | Happy and calm
test: Which of these best matches «agility training»? | *Training to move quickly and easily | Drawing with chalk | Reading long books | Sleeping in the sun
exam: Which is the correct comparative form of agile? | *more agile | agile more | agilest | agiler
